CM_ "1.0.0 - Iinitial Release";
CM_ BU_ ECP_Commanding_Node "Electronic control module in charge of controlling and coordinating the operation of a hybrid propulsion system.";
CM_ BO_ 2566650813 "Electrified Accessory Power Electronics Coolant Fan 1 Status
The status of electrified Accessory: Power Electronics Coolant Fan 1.   See PGN 30720 for the corresponding command message.";
CM_ SG_ 2566650813 Pwr "Calculated electrical power consumed by the Power Electronics Coolant Fan 1.";
CM_ SG_ 2566650813 CtrlTemp "A temperature measured and reported by the device.  It may be used for direct or remote (by another controller) control of the Fan 1.  For example, this may be the temperature of the fluid flowing through the Fan 1, or some other temperature ...";
CM_ SG_ 2566650813 MotorSpd "Motor Speed of the Power Electronics Coolant Fan 1.";
CM_ SG_ 2566650813 EnableStatus "Enable and direction status of the Power Electronics Coolant Fan 1 system or component.

00b = Accessory Motor Off
01b = Accessory Motor On - Normal, Forward, or Default Direction
10b = Accessory Motor On - Reverse Direction
11b = Not available";
CM_ BO_ 2557984188 "Electrified Accessory Power Electronics Coolant Fan 1 Command
The command message to the electrified accessory: Power Electronics Coolant Fan 1.  See PGN 64508 for the corresponding status message.";
CM_ SG_ 2557984188 PercentSpdCmd "Speed command to the Power Electronics Coolant Fan 1 in percentage of maximum speed.
Note: Both Speed Command and Percent Speed Command cannot be used at the same time.  Always set the unused speed command to Not Available.  If both commands are ...";
CM_ SG_ 2557984188 EnableCmd "Enable and direction command to the Power Electonics Coolant Fan 1.

00b = Accessory Motor Off
01b = Accessory Motor On Normal/Default Direction
10b = Accessory Motor On Reverse Direction
11b = Don't Care/Take no action";
